## Context

Child of master ticket 0660. R10 permits one disclosed, one-time model-weight
download, while `R10-no-egress` currently fails on every DNS lookup or
off-machine connection. The committed cold-cache evidence therefore counts the
permitted model host as part of a red. `DECISIONS.md` already records the open
choice among changing the specification, changing the product, or changing the
assertion. This child must not make that choice itself.

## Actions

- Obtain and record the author's ruling in `DECISIONS.md` first.
- Propagate only that ruling's consequences into SPEC.md, the assertion,
  fail-controls, README standing and affected tickets.
- If the exception remains, identify it positively and prove its disclosure and
  one-time character; do not whitelist all traffic sharing an address, process
  or time window.
- If the zero-call clause remains, separate its verdict from the narrower
  library-text/query custody promise so one red is not reported as the other.

## Test

- [ ] A permitted model acquisition reaches the ruling's intended state.
- [ ] Telemetry, update checks and data-bearing calls to the same infrastructure
      remain independently red where the ruling requires it.
- [ ] Missing destination or payload attribution cannot become PASS.
- [ ] Warm and cold cache arms prove which path actually ran.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The ruling is recorded before normative or scoring changes.
- [ ] Every affected prose and executable clause uses the same boundary.
- [ ] Each classification has a one-purpose red or positive control.
- [ ] Real-target warm/cold evidence is committed.
- [ ] `make check` and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
